{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>קרבו.</b> An imperative from the heavy [causative] stem with dagesh, on the pattern of ברכו יי (Judges 5:2)." "<b>עצומותיכם.</b> Like 'your dispute,' and likewise ובין עצומים יפריד (Proverbs 18:18). It is also possible that it is from the root עצום, and then it is a plural noun."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {0 "Resolved the divine name יי as YHWH per protocol; retained Ibn Ezra's grammatical term הכבד as 'heavy [causative] stem.'"}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:24.615889784Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}